# Runtime dependencies — DIRECT ones only, with the intent behind each bound.
#
# This file is hand-written; `requirements.txt` is GENERATED from it and pins
# every version, transitive dependencies included. Never edit requirements.txt
# by hand — regenerate it:
#
#     .venv/bin/pip-compile requirements.in
#     .venv/bin/pip-compile requirements-dev.in
#
# Why the split (abstract vs. concrete dependencies): this file says what the
# project needs and why; the generated one says exactly what to install. Without
# the second, `>=` means a fresh install resolves to whatever exists on build
# day, and two builds of the same commit can differ. That is not theoretical —
# `openai>=1.6.0` quietly resolved to 3.0.0, which raises from the client
# constructor and broke CI weeks after the code was written.

